# GitHub Workflow (compulsory)

All work follows this sequence. Scope: all work.

## 1. Plan doc first

Before code changes, create or update a plan doc in `docs/<scope>/plans/`.
The plan doc is the source of intake, scope, and acceptance criteria.

Plan doc must include:
```
## Background
## Expected outcome
## Acceptance criteria
## Possible solution(s)
## References
```

## 2. Branch

Checkout/create branch from `main` using `fix/<scope>-slug` or `feat/<scope>-slug`.

## 3. Plan alignment

When an agent creates an execution plan (e.g. todo list), persist it in the active plan doc before starting work.

## 4. Work

Make changes within the bounded context defined by the active plan doc scope.
When contracts change: run `pnpm turbo run generate --filter=@forge/graphql` in the same PR and tick "Regeneration Required: yes" in PR template.

## 5. Commits

Produce a series of commits—one per small block of work. Each commit must use conventional format (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:` etc.). Atomic and reviewable.

**Before committing**, verify the current branch's PR is not already merged:
```
gh pr list --repo JesusFilm/forge --head "$(git branch --show-current)" --state merged --json number
```
If the result is non-empty, **stop** — do not commit or push. Create a new branch from `main` instead.

## 6. PR

Open PR targeting `main`. Use title format `type(scope): description`. Fill PR template (Summary, Contracts Changed, Regeneration Required, Validation). Include the active plan doc path in PR description.

**Creating/updating PRs with multiline bodies:** Never pass `\n` escape sequences in MCP tool string parameters — they render as literal text. Always use `gh` CLI with a HEREDOC:
```
gh pr create --title "type(scope): description" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
...
EOF
)"
```
Same applies to `gh pr edit`.

## Resolving merge conflicts

**Never rebase a feature branch to resolve PR merge conflicts.** Use `git merge` instead:
```
git fetch upstream main && git merge upstream/main --no-edit
```
For `pnpm-lock.yaml` conflicts: `git checkout --theirs pnpm-lock.yaml && pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile`, then stage and commit.

## 7. Checks

Ensure all CI checks pass before marking work complete. Use `mcp_GitHub_pull_request_read` with `method: get_status` to verify. Re-run or fix failures.

## 8. Post check passing

Resolve all review comments with follow-up—fix the issue or explain why it doesn't need to be addressed. Add a PR comment summarizing how each comment was handled (fixed or why not addressed).
